# Wedding website – project conventions

## Structure
- **Sections** (Hero, Schedule, Location, Parking, RsvpEmbed) live in `src/components/` and use shared motion variants from `src/theme/motionVariants.js`.
- **Data**: `src/data/site.js` (wedding details), `src/data/copy.js` (UI strings), `src/data/navLinks.js` (footer nav), `src/data/schedule.js` (timeline).
- **Constants**: Use `src/constants.js` for magic values (e.g. `COUNTDOWN_INTERVAL_MS`, `SECTION_IDS`). Use `src/theme/tokens.js` for `duration`, `easing`, and `layout` (spacing classes).
- **Types**: JSDoc types live in `src/types.js`; reference them in data files with `@type {import('../types').Site}` etc.

## When adding or changing UI
- Add or edit **copy** in `src/data/copy.js`; use `copy.key` in components. Do not hardcode section titles or button labels in JSX.
- Add **nav links** in `src/data/navLinks.js` (id, href, labelKey). Keep `SECTION_IDS` in `constants.js` in sync with section `id` attributes.
- Use **layout** from `src/theme/tokens.js` for section padding, viewport margin, min-heights (e.g. `layout.sectionPadding`, `layout.viewportMargin`).

## Animations
- Use **motion variants** from `src/theme/motionVariants.js`: `getHeroContainer()`, `getSectionContainerReveal()`, `sectionItem`, `scheduleItem`, `heroItem`, `timelineDot`.
- Pass `custom={{ reduced: shouldReduceMotion }}` on section containers so reduced-motion preference is respected (zero stagger/delay).

## Icons and components
- Add **icons** in `src/components/Icons.jsx` as named exports; use them in components instead of inline SVGs.
- **Barrel**: Export public components from `src/components/index.js`; import from `'./components'` in App.

## General
- Prefer existing constants and shared modules over new magic numbers or duplicated logic.
- Keep section ids and nav link ids aligned so anchor navigation works.
